WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.020
It's Sendai...

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:05.780
N-No!

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:06.580
I'm okay-!

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.130
Ow!

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.480
Ah! Hey! Don't leave the stage yet!

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.410
Natsu! Help me!

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.570
Help me, Natsu!

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:51.820
I'm hoping that she becomes
unable to live outside the village!

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:00.480
I went to pray that the idol contest
would go well for Machi.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.930
So why did I say those things
to the mountain gods?

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.530
Argh, geez!

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.330
I'm taking them back!

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.900
It'll be bad if something
bad happens to Machi!

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.830
I'm going to talk to the mountain gods
and recant what I said!

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.340
It's from Yoshio.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:25.330
Did you guys get in okay?

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.280
Natsu, Machi's gone!

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.690
Hm? Machi's gonna what?

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.090
You mean she's gonna win
the contest for sure?

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.030
Is that right?!

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:34.700
What the hell are you talking
about at a time like this?!

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.480
Hm? What do you mean?

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.900
I said Machi is gone!

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.450
Huh?

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.190
Machi is...

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.170
Machi is gone?!

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.130
Whaaaaaaaat?!

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:25.140
Machi got so worked up
during the rehearsal.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.850
This is on a bigger scale than
the event at the rest area, you know.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.640
So she was really nervous.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.560
I won't participate.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.440
I'm going back... to the village.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.980
I'm going home! I'm going home!

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.530
This is happening because of
what I said to the mountain gods...

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:43.700
Hiiko was taken by a security guard, too.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.490
I'm in such a bind.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.200
What time is Machi supposed
to be on the stage?

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.620
The opening part will start
in about 20 minutes...

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.790
...but if it comes down to it,
she could skip that.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.750
So she needs to appear...

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.920
...in about two and a half hours, I think.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.340
I know telling you won't do
anything but make you worry...

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.180
...but I wondered what you
would do in this situation.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.180
Can you think of any place
where Machi could be?

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.480
Hm? Are you listening, Natsu?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.150
Matsu-san's House

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:27.990
Matsu-san!

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.290
Oh, it's you, Natsu-sama.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.460
Have you had a drink today, Matsu-san?

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:39.050
Today's batch turned out just right,
so I was about to start.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.760
Would you like to join me and
have some too, Natsu-sama-

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.380
Could you drive me?!

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:43.970
Machi is...

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:45.340
Machi is...!

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.180
Natsu-sama!

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.980
Hang on tight!

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.440
Machi!

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:05.030
Excuse me, have you seen a
middle-school girl dressed as a miko?

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.740
Excuse me, have you seen a...

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.120
Sheesh!

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.700
How dare they...!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.500
Hey, Hiiko!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.790
Did you find Machi?

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.540
No, I can't find her anywhere.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.260
Excuse me.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:23.380
Yes?

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.300
Is this the place where I can request
a missing child announcement?

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:28.840
Yes, it is.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.300
How old is the child?

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.220
It's a 14-year-old girl.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:33.980
Huh?

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.770
What?

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.230
If she hears her name called
in a missing child announcement,

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.150
she won't wanna come out even more!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.700
What else can we do?!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.660
We can't find her anywhere!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.580
It wasn't meant to be after all.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:55.160
She's met more people in this single day
than in her whole life up to now.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:08.220
I should have been more considerate
towards Machi's feelings.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.970
I should have stopped her.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.180
I wish I could go to Sendai...

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.260
They why don't you go?

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:16.980
Oh, that's right!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.150
Natsu? What's going on?

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:29.110
I searched for Machi's
current location using GPS.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.490
I have her general location.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:32.870
Really?!

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.080
Where?!

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.910
A short distance from the station...

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:39.290
Maybe in a department store?

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.330
She went to a place like that?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.750
Thank you, Natsu!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:53.390
According to Natsu,
Machi should be somewhere in here.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.260
Yeah.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.600
Let's split up and look for her.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:56.310
Okay!

00:06:58.430 --> 00:06:59.350
Machi!

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.770
Machi!

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.690
Hey!

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.320
Machi!

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.280
Machi!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.400
Sheesh...

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.200
Where did she go?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:19.960
Did you find her?

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.130
Maybe she's already gone somewhere else.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.420
It's about time for the opening part
of the contest to start.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:27.880
We've got-

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.630
Hey...

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:31.550
Why don't you give up?

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.300
Why are you being so obstinate?

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.890
It's obvious she really doesn't wanna do it.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.190
Is revitalizing the village that important?

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.070
Yeah, it is important.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:49.320
Huh?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:53.200
Since Kumade Village is becoming more
depopulated every year, it lacks energy.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.570
Revitalization means giving
a light to the village.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:59.950
The future of the entire Kumade Village
depends on this project!

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.750
You jerk!

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:05.580
Are you saying that makes
it okay to sacrifice her?!

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.130
My mom made that miko outfit.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.090
You know the old tale
of Kumade Village, right?

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:12.010
Natsu helped her practice her performance.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.840
The story about village maidens
being offered as sacrifices...

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.010
Matsu-san made such a big banner.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.760
That's just a superstition to trick children!

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:18.430
And you helped her train!

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.720
But if you put that story in the current time...

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:24.980
Everyone in the village is rooting
for her and has high hopes for her!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:23.020
...don't you think it's talking about miko,
who have shamanistic powers?

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.100
I know it's hard on her...

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:29.400
This village revitalization project
is every villager's wish!

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:29.610
...but I want her to do her best as
a village representative for everyone's sake.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.900
No matter how you look at it,
that interpretation doesn't make sense!

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.910
Is that why you have been hung up on her?

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.700
Suit yourself.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.410
So, Hiiko, please help me find Machi.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:41.830
I will...

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:43.660
But...

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.540
...instead of forcing her to be in the contest,

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.670
let her decide in the end.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.630
Whatever she chooses to do, it's her life.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.880
As her manager, I want to
ask you to promise me that.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:56.590
Okay.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.420
Sheesh.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.640
We're in a hurry!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:40.470
This isn't good, really...

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.680
Matsu-san, I'm getting off here.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:46.480
What?

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.980
I guess...

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.320
We're almost there, but...

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.320
I'm sorry.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:58.990
Thank you.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.950
Well then, I'll get going now.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.830
Ah, hold on.

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:04.950
This!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.670
This is...

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:11.170
Please let her know everyone
in the village supports her, too!

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.590
Oh, you look good in it, Natsu-sama!

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.810
Well then, see you later!

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:23.760
Be careful!

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.810
So I told her...

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.360
Yeah?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.270
Hm?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.530
Did I just see a bear running by?

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.110
Huh?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.740
There's no way that a bear
would be around here.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:48.910
Everyone in the village is rooting
for her and has high hopes for her!

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.290
He's right.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.750
I have to try harder for everyone's sake.

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.340
Let her decide in the end.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.340
Whatever she chooses to do, it's her life.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:03.760
But...

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.140
...this is just too much for me...

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:14.520
Um...

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.400
Are you an idol?

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:19.190
What?

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.990
You're going to be in the idol contest, right?

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:23.490
That's cool!

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.620
Well... um...

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.790
Please shake my hands!

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.090
Good luck!

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.840
Thank you.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:39.840
Yuki!

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.180
Let's go!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:42.890
Okay!

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.140
See you!

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.600
Mom, I met an idol!

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.730
Oh, good for you!

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.730
I wanna become an idol, too!

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.610
In order to become an idol...

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:04.160
Thank you very much for
your wonderful performance!

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.240
Next is contestant 14.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.160
She's from Yamagata Prefecture.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.040
Did you find her?!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.040
No.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.290
Did you check the waiting room?

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:12.580
Yeah, many times.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.540
I want these feelings to reach you!

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:19.090
They're number 14, so after this one
and the next one, it's her turn.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.640
The contest venue should be around here...

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:27.930
...but-

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:30.220
Ah!

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.890
I'm a bear!

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:35.230
If I'm here, it'll create a panic
at the contest venue!

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:38.480
The event will be canceled!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.990
How can I get closer?

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:42.990
Excuse me...

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.990
Can we take a picture with you?

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:48.330
Shoot!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.490
They noticed me!

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.000
This is cool!

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.250
It's one of those talking ones!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.080
This one is the most realistic bear
character we've ever seen, isn't it?!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.380
He looks cute in the happi coat!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.290
Hm...?

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:59.920
They think that I'm a mascot
character... maybe?

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:58.670
Yep!

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:01.630
Oh, sure.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.180
You can take a picture with me... bear.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.640
All right!

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.470
Thank you very much!

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:13.140
Your coat of hair looks real, too!

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:13.770
What?!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:17.100
Y-Yes, I go for realism, bear.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.730
Whoa!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.520
Well then, if you'll excuse me, bear...

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.070
His speech and mouth
movements were in sync.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:26.780
I bet it's the type that has
a built-in fan, since it's hot inside.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:30.580
At this rate, I might be okay...

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.210
Mom, it's a bear!

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:45.130
That was contestant number 15,
the Namahage Idol, Non Non-chan!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.720
Thank you very much!

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.390
Well then, let's have the next performer!

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.310
Contestant 16 is the Kumade Village Idol!

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.650
This is cool!

00:13:58.650 --> 00:13:59.900
Sorry.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:01.730
Later, okay?

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.360
Amayadori Machi-san!

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.110
Hm?

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.200
Erm, okay.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.080
Well, we'll change our plan.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.040
Hm? Machi-chan...?

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:17.920
Machi-chan...?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:20.080
Contestant 17 is...

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.380
Machi!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.550
She...

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:26.630
Machi-chan!

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:27.510
Machi-chan!!

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:29.430
Ah... Uhm...

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.470
Amayadori Machi-san... right?

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:34.970
Machi!

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:36.980
Okay!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:39.520
Then, first, please introduce yourself.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:51.870
Uhm...

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.490
I'm from Kumade Village, Amayadori Machi.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.000
Machi-Machi-Machi!

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.750
Machi, Machi, Machi, Machi...!

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.920
That's a pretty costume.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.580
Is that a miko outfit?

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:06.760
Well then, it's time for her performance!

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.230
She's a country bumpkin!

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:24.770
Throw rocks at her!

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.610
Go home! Go home!

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:28.860
This isn't good.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:32.660
Machi...

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.160
Machi...

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:39.750
Kumaan!

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:44.630
Natsu!

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.000
She's...

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.220
Machi...

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.270
You want to go to school in the city?

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.270
I'm going.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:42.640
No matter what.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:46.060
I'm sick of this village!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.320
I've decided...

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.530
that I'll promote Kumade's nameko!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:53.860
Go buy a HEATTECH item at Uniqlo. Natsu.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.570
I have to pick an outfit to wear to Uniqlo!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:58.240
You bought an item from HEATTECH didn't you?

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.200
I feel...

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.660
like I can't do anything myself.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.250
That's a total failure, then.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:09.630
Everyone has things they aren't good at.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.510
I'm sorry for forcing you to do
something you couldn't handle.

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:15.930
I'm sorry for saying mean things to you.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.090
Natsu.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:22.060
I don't care... what sort of beating I have to take...

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:32.440
Machi...

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:34.780
I guess...

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.660
...she isn't a small child anymore...

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.370
Yoshio!

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:04.890
Go home!

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.440
Go home!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.480
Go home!

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:09.600
You country bumpkin!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.480
Stop it!

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.320
Throw rocks at her!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:16.070
Stop iiiit!

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.360
It's 400 years too early for you!

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.370
Next is the weather forecast.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:23.910
Tomorrow will be...

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.370
Oh, hey, Machi!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.160
Machi!

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.370
How was Sendai?

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.790
I heard that it was amazing!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.500
She received enthusiastic applause!

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.710
It was a huge success!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.300
They threw rocks at me.

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:37.510
Huh?

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.260
They told me to go home.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:44.310
They called me "country bumpkin," too!

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.930
Wait, Machi...

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:47.680
I...

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:49.270
I won't go...

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:52.560
I won't go to high school in the city!

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.610
What? What? Whaaaaat?!

00:18:58.530 --> 00:18:59.360
Machi...

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:03.700
You aren't going to high school in the city?

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.160
Throw rocks at her!

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.620
Throw rocks!

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:13.630
I... I... I... won't... go...

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.340
Machi!

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:22.890
Yep, yep.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.220
You're right!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.510
That's a good idea!

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:28.730
You don't have to think
about difficult stuff anymore!

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:31.060
You don't have to do it, either!

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:34.400
I don't... have to... think about it?

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.570
That's right!

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:40.030
I don't... have to do... anything?

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.110
That's right!

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.700
They won't... throw rocks at me?

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.120
They won't!

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.290
I see...

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.710
Let's eat something delicious today!

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.920
Natsu... I...

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.630
Is it okay...? Is it really okay?

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.420
Yes, that's okay!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.260
Natsu... Thank you!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.470
I love you!

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.390
I love you, too!

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:12.730
I heard that Machi-chan didn't come out
even after the MC person called her name.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:15.650
I bet Yoshio and Hibiki's
hearts went pitter-patter.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.400
In any case...

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:21.190
I'm so glad... really...

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:26.200
I said that Machi-chan has
the aptitude to be an idol, didn't I?

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:28.290
I don't recall you saying that.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.410
I always said that, didn't I?!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.160
That's sexual harassment!

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:42.380
Hey, pops!

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:43.630
Two miso, please.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:48.220
I haven't seen you two here together
in a long time, what's up?

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.510
Shut up!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:51.520
Geez...

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.600
We're having the event
wrap-up party here?!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:55.650
Now, now.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.730
Eat as much as you like today.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.990
At any rate, she thought people
would throw rocks at her?

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:05.160
Just how timid is she?

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:07.620
How did she come to that conclusion?

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.540
You can't make light of
what Machi says, though.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:15.420
I went to Sendai on business a little while ago.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:23.010
I don't remember why, but a Sendai
person threw a rock at me.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.590
Yeah, he did.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:29.260
Are they pretty hotheaded?

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:30.430
Hmm...

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.310
I wonder why he did it...

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:35.310
I didn't do anything...

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:38.190
No, I bet you did something, Yoshio.

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:42.150
But I won't give up!

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.860
I'll promote the village more
so that many people will visit us!

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:49.280
I'll make it Japan's number-one village
where people can live active lives!

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.040
He is... pretty passionate.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:57.790
Geez...

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:00.380
What do I do with you?

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:07.590
Receipt Stamp

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:07.720
Here.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:07.590
Kumai

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:09.260
Thank you.

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:10.680
Thank you very much!

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:15.730
Whoa!

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:17.560
This is delicious!

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:20.020
I had it delivered, it's Zunda Mont Blanc.

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:23.020
Zunda Mont Blanc is delicious!

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:26.990
With this tablet, you can order
anything and have it delivered.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:30.780
Tablet is candy with
a minty-fresh flavor, right?

00:22:30.780 --> 00:22:32.280
Can you eat it?

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:33.740
Of course not.

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.450
You order things from
an internet shopping site, Machi.

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:37.910
"Saito"?

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:40.670
Internet Saito is wonderful!

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:43.880
So does Saito-san's shop sell everything?

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:45.300
It's not like that!

00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:47.920
Shops around the country
ship things to us!

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:51.850
Does Saito-san deliver them?

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:53.180
Isn't that a lot of work?

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:55.350
That's okay!

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:57.930
You don't have to think about it!

00:22:57.930 --> 00:22:59.730
Geez...

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:03.570
Tell me, Natsu!

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.360
It tickles, Machi!

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:06.860
Take this! Take this!

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:12.320
Take this! Take this!

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:16.830
Take this!

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:31.180
Kumamiko-chan!

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:34.760
I'm hungry...

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:37.060
I'm hungry!

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:41.770
Here's the yomogi daifuku
purchased at a supermarket.

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:44.440
If you spread it on a piece of bread...

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:46.940
...toast it in a toaster oven...

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:49.610
...put butter on it and eat it...

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:53.160
...it tastes good.
